30,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Rin,,The station block's bin house is a trap! It smells way worse in the summer because you can't wash it. We shouldn't just build a box!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I've looked at the costs. Last year's shelters were quite expensive, and we're already spending over thirty thousand yen annually just on maintenance. We must be careful.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's worse than I thought. One household is doing almost all the complaining, and nobody wants to be the ""trash police."" We're on the verge of a total freeze.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"Here's the catch: the next lane spends nearly fifty minutes per shift. If we do a rotation, that's a lot of unpaid labor for a few of us.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The measurements show a clear disparity. One frontage is far more suitable than others, but the ward's filing requirements make moving the site a bureaucratic nightmare.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Midori, if it's expensive, maybe we can find a cheaper way that doesn't smell? I don't want a fancy box that stinks!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, exactly. If we spend a lot on a shelter, we might not be able to afford the maintenance. We need a low-cost, sustainable solution.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, if the ward's requirements are a nightmare, maybe we shouldn't move the site. Moving it might just shift the resentment to a different neighbor.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, exactly. And if we just ""rotate"" the duty, the person who answers the phone first always ends up doing the heavy lifting. We need a time-capped plan.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, ignoring the location doesn't solve the inequality. One person has had the bins at their gate for years. That is a spatial tax they've paid alone.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But if we move it to someone else's gate, they'll be sad too! Can't we just make it easier to clean?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I'm worried about the budget. Some of us can't afford a huge one-time payment for a new shelter, even with a subsidy.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's be honest: we're not just fighting about bins; we're fighting about respect. If we force a move, we might break the neighborhood permanently.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"Respect is great, but time is money. If the truck arrives at 7:40, we're asking people to sacrifice their sleep. That's a high price for ""respect.""","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"Respect is also acknowledging that one person's frontage has been occupied for years. A ""fair"" plan that leaves the site unchanged is not fair.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,I just want it to not be gross in August! Let's pick the one that's easiest to scrub!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,I'll support any plan that doesn't put a heavy financial burden on any single household. Let's keep the costs minimal.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I'll vote for the option that minimizes the need for us to police each other. The less we have to argue about ""late bags,"" the better.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm voting for the one that has the clearest, most limited time commitment. No more ""volunteer"" roles that turn into full-time jobs.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I will vote for the option that addresses the spatial burden. If the site doesn't move or rotate, the cost must be offset.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
