59,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I hate Option C! I saw that bin house—it's a stinky box! Option B sounds like an adventure, moving the bins around!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Option C is too expensive. Even with a subsidy, the upfront cost is too high for some budgets. Option A is the most affordable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option B is a recipe for disaster. Imagine the arguments when the bins move to a house that's ""too clean."" Option A is safer for our relationships.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"Option A is a nightmare. ""Overseeing"" it for fifty minutes a shift? That's exactly the kind of labor that falls on the most helpful person.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A and C both leave the burden on one household's frontage. Option B is the only one that ensures spatial equality over time.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@May, but if we move the bins in Option B, maybe the smell doesn't stay in one place for too long?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Asuka, I understand the spatial burden, but Option B might lead to more maintenance costs if we have to move equipment. Option A is free.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, spatial equality is a mathematical goal, but social peace is a human one. Option B will just create five different people who are angry.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Midori, ""free"" is a lie. It costs time. Option B is better because the burden is visible and scheduled, not a vague ""supervision"" duty.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, social peace built on the silent sacrifice of one neighbor is an illusion. Option B is the only logical way to distribute the physical cost.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm still scared of the stinky box! I'll vote for the moving bins because it's more exciting and fairer for the houses!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I really can't support C. Between A and B, A is the most financially stable for everyone. I'll vote for A to keep costs at zero.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I'm sticking with A. It's the least disruptive. We can figure out the ""supervision"" part without turning into a police state.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, you say that now, but you'll be the one answering the phone when the bins aren't moved. I'm voting B. It's a clear, timed rotation.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,Option A is a failure of fairness. Option C is a permanent burden on one person. Option B is the only choice that treats all frontages as equal.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,Let's just vote! I hope we don't get the stinky box!,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,I hope we choose the one that doesn't leave anyone struggling to pay.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,Let's just hope we can still talk to each other by next month.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"As long as I'm not the only one doing the work, I'm happy.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,Logic dictates that the physical burden must be shared. I'm ready.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
